etym:
Borrowed from Sanskrit आमात्य (āmātya, “from or belonging to the same house or family; companion (of a royal person); minister; councillor; etc”).
Cognate with Pali amacca, whence Thai อมัจจะ.
Cognate also with Old Khmer °ʼamātya, °ʼāmātya;

